Third-party parts keep their own licences:
- three.js 0.187 and its examples (GLTFLoader, post-processing passes, RoomEnvironment, Sky,
  RoundedBoxGeometry), bundled into index.html: MIT, Copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
- Build and test tools, not shipped: Vite and vite-plugin-singlefile (MIT), Playwright
  (Apache-2.0), imagetracerjs (Unlicense, used by scripts/trace.mjs), pngjs (MIT). Blender and
  ImageMagick were used as tools to prepare the 3D model and the traced pictures; nothing from
  them is shipped.

The cabin, the garden, the procedural textures and the galloping dog (src/three/lib/) come from
Spot-light HD (github.com/Gitguy268/spot-light-hd) by the same author, MIT. The vector gallop
(src/vector/traced/gallop.js) is traced from renders of that dog and is MIT too.

Pictures of Spot that are NOT covered by the MIT licence (ask before reusing them):
- assets/spot-blanket.glb: an AI-generated 3D model of the author's dog in a blanket, made for
  the author, with its textures resized for the web (blender/prepare_scan.py).
- assets/spot-bandana.webp: an AI-generated portrait of the author's dog, shown as the framed
  photo above the fireplace.
- src/vector/traced/spot-blanket.js: vector shapes traced (scripts/trace.mjs) from an
  AI-generated portrait of the author's dog.
- index.html embeds all three, and the screenshots in docs/ and the screen saver thumbnails in
  macos/ show them.

The page loads nothing from the network and uses the system's fonts.
